=head1 DESCRIPTION

The settings for Amazon Pinpoint analytics configuration. With an
analytics configuration, your application can collect user-activity
metrics for user notifications with a Amazon Pinpoint campaign.

Amazon Pinpoint isn't available in all Amazon Web Services Regions. For
a list of available Regions, see Amazon Cognito and Amazon Pinpoint
Region availability
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-pinpoint-integration.html#cognito-user-pools-find-region-mappings).

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 ApplicationArn => Str

The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of an Amazon Pinpoint project that you
want to connect to your user pool app client. Amazon Cognito publishes
events to the Amazon Pinpoint project that C<ApplicationArn> declares.
You can also configure your application to pass an endpoint ID in the
C<AnalyticsMetadata> parameter of sign-in operations. The endpoint ID
is information about the destination for push notifications


=head2 ApplicationId => Str

Your Amazon Pinpoint project ID.


=head2 ExternalId => Str

The external ID
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-user_externalid.html)
of the role that Amazon Cognito assumes to send analytics data to
Amazon Pinpoint.


=head2 RoleArn => Str

The ARN of an Identity and Access Management role that has the
permissions required for Amazon Cognito to publish events to Amazon
Pinpoint analytics.


=head2 UserDataShared => Bool

If C<UserDataShared> is C<true>, Amazon Cognito includes user data in
the events that it publishes to Amazon Pinpoint analytics.



